<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_SumpFauna.xml                          RM_TheSump · SUMP_FAUNA_ROSTER_1
  ============================================================================
  The nine invented Sump fauna rows per
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/sump_fauna_roster_2026-09-24.md: sump-mouse
  (row 1, real def replacing RUT_Placeholder_SumpMouseRace/RUT_Placeholder_
  SumpMouse — both retired, this file's row is now the real content), gulveth,
  the thrummel family (thrummel/warden/broodmother), brommet, dredgel,
  skarrid, and skellarn (the ruled real-flight stilt-legged flier).

  🔴 Eviction scope, per the design doc's own §7 and the owner's standing
  "evictions are stopped" ruling (2026-09-22): the doc marks replacing today's
  4 donor Alpha Animals rows (AA_TarGuzzler/AA_Bumbledrone/
  AA_BumbledroneHierophant/AA_BumbledroneQueen) with gulveth/thrummel/warden/
  broodmother as **PROPOSED for the Sump's own sitting, executed by nobody
  here**. This pass builds all four defs in full but does NOT touch
  RM_TheSump_Biome.xml's existing donor wildAnimals rows — only rows with no
  existing donor slot to evict (mouse, brommet, dredgel, skarrid, skellarn)
  are wired into wildAnimals this pass. Whoever runs the Sump's biome sitting
  rules on the other four.

  Sump-mouse is the one exception to "no existing slot": its placeholder was
  never wired into wildAnimals at all (its own header: "NOT added to RUT_
  Sump's own wildAnimals list") and was explicitly built as a mechanism stub
  awaiting "the roster pass" (same header) — replacing it is this item's own
  named job, not an eviction of anything live.

  Mechanism scope — deferred, per the roster doc's own status column (mirrors
  SUMP_FLORA_ROSTER_1's precedent of deferring NEW/PARTIAL placement and
  behaviour mechanisms out of a roster-def item): mouse/skellarn free tar-
  crossing on landing (one shared implementation, UNMEASURED which is
  cheapest), thrummel mound + defend-radius comp (vanilla Hive/
  CompSpawnerPawn reskin feasibility UNMEASURED), skarrid's mobile dread-field
  registration (dread field itself already exists), and dredgel's dig-site
  attract-mode wander bias. All four are content-complete as ordinary wild
  animals now; their bespoke behaviours are follow-on Sump-mechanics work.

  Bodies: mouse/QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail (kept from the placeholder);
  gulveth/QuadrupedAnimalWithHoovesAndHump (barge-back register, same body
  family this repo's own big placid grazers use); thrummel family/
  QuadrupedAnimalWithPaws (round, furred, per the roster's own "furred
  bumbler" flavour text, not an insectoid body); brommet/
  QuadrupedAnimalWithHooves (small wool grazer); dredgel/Crab (long, low,
  many-legged sifter — the closest vanilla body to the roster's own
  silhouette brief); skarrid/TurtleLike (flat armoured ambusher); skellarn/
  Bird (the biome's one flier).

  Art: none of the nine has existing generated art anywhere (registry.jsonl/
  done/_artsrc searched this pass, 0 hits on all nine names — sanity-probed
  against "graniteslug", 30 hits, so the search itself is live). All nine
  reference bespoke texPaths under TheSump/Textures/Things/Pawn/Animal/ that
  do not exist yet; DEPLOY_HOLD'd, fill_queue.py jobs filed
  (infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/sump_fauna.csv), south/east/north facings
  per generating-rimworld-sprites. No dessicatedBodyGraphicData on any of the
  nine — same posture this mod's own RM_FleetFlier/RM_Skerrel (Greentide/
  TheForge) already ship for bespoke-pending-art creatures.

  Flight (RM_Skellarn only): real flight per the standing rule (owner,
  2026-09-19) — MaxFlightTime/FlightCooldown are the CORE stat pair
  (Pawn_FlightTracker.CanEverFly), not a bool. canLeaveMapFlying deliberately
  OMITTED: the doc's own one-home note says it lairs in the outer ring's
  brindeth scrub, no migration mechanism claimed. No
  flyingAnimationFramePathPrefix/-FrameCount: frames are OWED later (roster
  doc's own art row) and must never block flight — GetBestFlyAnimation
  returns null with none set and it flies plainly, which is correct at this
  stage. Numbers (~10 MaxFlightTime, ~5 FlightCooldown, ~2.2
  flightSpeedFactor) are the roster doc's own "❓" estimates, landed as real
  values since a def field cannot ship a question mark.
  ============================================================================
-->
